From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: nsscc-qca8k: keep QCA8386 access clocks on

The QCA8386 NSS clock controller is exposed as an MDIO child.  Its clock
consumers can probe after the kernel's unused-clock pass, while the switch
MHT window must remain clocked for the first DSA ID read.  Mark the access
and integrated-PHY clock chain critical so clk_disable_unused cannot shut it
down between NSSCC registration and the MDIO/DSA children.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-qca8k.c
